Viewer: window shapes keep their true proportions, the whole set fitted to the stream once (2026-10-22).

Each shape was fitted on its own to at least 1280 on the long side, so a split screen's third grew to
1280 like the full window, and CarPlay, which lays out by physical width, showed both the same amount.
A shape is now the window's CSS size times the pixels used (windowShape), and areaPlan fits the whole
set with one factor into 1280..max (2560 with a fast decoder). Stored shapes move to f50-window-shapes;
the old f50-view-areas records were already fitted and are dropped. Tests: thirds, a 2x Mac at 2560,
and a small page alone.

